<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#druk-gyalpo">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Druk Gyalpo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dragon King</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Druk Gyalpo, 'Dragon King', is the title of the head of state of Bhutan. The hereditary monarchy was established in 1907, when an assembly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punakha">Punakha</a> elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ugyen-wangchuck">Ugyen Wangchuck</a> as the first Druk Gyalpo, ending the old dual system of civil and religious rulers. Five kings of the Wangchuck dynasty have reigned since, and in 2008 the office became that of a constitutional monarch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/druk-gyalpo.jpg" alt="Druk Gyalpo" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 首相官邸ホームページ · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jigme_Khesar_Namgyel_Wangchuck_at_the_Enthronement_of_Naruhito.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
